-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a9e8fd35-6034-4b6c-ab78-a8fe138fd983
-- title:
--   The combined source and reporting resource need is polynomial
-- statement:
--   For input length $n$ and absolute-value bound $U$, let $R_{\mathrm{source}}(n,U)$ be the encoded-color pipeline's resource need, and $R_{\mathrm{setup}}(n,U)$ the reporting-setup need. Each need records a word bound, allocated cell count, and call-depth allowance. Define their combined need by adding the word and cell components, and adding both depth components plus two.
--
--   There exist natural constants $s,k$, independent of $n,U$, such that all three components satisfy
--   $$R_{\mathrm{combined}}(n,U).\mathrm{word},\quad R_{\mathrm{combined}}(n,U).\mathrm{cells},\quad R_{\mathrm{combined}}(n,U).\mathrm{depth}\ \le\ 2^s((n+1)(U+1))^k.$$
--
--   This proves polynomial resource requirements for source construction followed by reporting initialization.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorReportingResources.lean#L45-L65

